## Initial Access Prerequisites

Submit these baseline entitlement requests via the corporate self-service portal so credentials provision in the background while you review the guides:

| Platform System | Entitlement Group | Required Purpose | Validation Command |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Enterprise GitHub** | `org-mobile-engineering` | Clone core repositories and templates | `ssh -T git@git.enterprise.internal` |
| **Artifact Registry** | `pkg-mobile-artifacts-read` | Pull shared Maven, CocoaPods & npm packages | `curl -I https://registry.enterprise.internal/health` |
| **Bitrise CI / CD** | `bitrise-mobile-engineers` | Trigger builds and inspect PR status | Bitrise dashboard console login |
| **Figma Design System** | `design-mobile-tokens` | Access unified UI components and design specs | Figma workspace project access |

---

:::caution[Foundational Platform Guardrails]
Keep these non-negotiable principles in mind as you progress through each track:

* **Strict Layered Separation:** UI components must only observe ViewModel state; direct repository or network calls from view layers are strictly prohibited.
* **Zero Plaintext Credentials:** API secrets, auth tokens, and certificates must always reside in secure storage (KeyStore / Keychain), never in source control.
* **Offline-First Resilience:** All features touching network endpoints must implement caching and Circuit Breaker resilience.
* **Automated Gate Compliance:** Every pull request must pass Danger PR Bot static analysis and unit test suites prior to merge.
:::




