:::tip[Ecosystem Topology]
The Enterprise Mobile Engineering Platform establishes a unified delivery framework across iOS, Android, and React Native. It standardizes common capabilities into shared infrastructure—including identity, networking resilience, automated gate inspections, and telemetry—enabling teams to focus on domain features.
:::

## Key Platform Capabilities

<CardGrid>
  <Card title="Client Stacks" icon="open-book">
    Jetpack Compose, SwiftUI, and React Native New Architecture with shared tokens.
  </Card>
  <Card title="CI/CD & Bitrise" icon="setting">
    Automated build runners, Danger PR inspections, and Fastlane deployment pipelines.
  </Card>
  <Card title="Release Gates" icon="warning">
    Automated coverage gates, Sauce Labs device regression, and NowSecure security scans.
  </Card>
  <Card title="Observability" icon="information">
    Datadog RUM telemetry, real-time crash alerting, and remote feature flag management.
  </Card>
</CardGrid>

---

## Platform Delivery Lifecycle

The Enterprise Mobile Platform follows a standardized delivery lifecycle from local feature creation through automated inspection, store distribution, and runtime production operations:

<MermaidZoom title="PLATFORM DELIVERY LIFECYCLE">

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Dev["Local Workstation & Development\n(IDEs, Templates & Internal SDKs)"]
    PR["GitHub Enterprise Pull Request"]

    Dev --> PR

    subgraph CI["Quality & Security (Bitrise CI Pipeline)"]
        Danger["Danger PR Code Checks"]
        Sauce["Sauce Labs Device Cloud"]
        NowSec["NowSecure SAST/DAST"]

        Danger --> Sauce --> NowSec
    end

    PR --> Danger

    subgraph Dist["Store Distribution"]
        PublicStore["Public App Stores\n(Google Play & Apple App Store)"]
        EnterpriseStore["Enterprise App Portal\n(Internal Distribution)"]
    end

    NowSec --> PublicStore
    NowSec --> EnterpriseStore

    subgraph Ops["Production Operations"]
        Users["Active Mobile Users"]
        Datadog["Datadog RUM Telemetry\n& Crash Alerts"]

        Users --> Datadog
    end

    PublicStore --> Users
    EnterpriseStore --> Users
```

</MermaidZoom>

* **Development:** Feature development executed in Android Studio, Xcode, or VS Code using enterprise templates and internal shared SDK packages.
* **Quality & Security:** Automated Bitrise CI triggers on every pull request, executing static Danger inspections, unit test suites, cloud device regression, and binary vulnerability scanning.
* **Distribution:** Automated deployment to public app stores (Apple App Store, Google Play Store) or private Enterprise App Distribution portals.
* **Operations:** Real-time production telemetry via Datadog RUM, crash report tracking, and remote emergency kill switches.

---

## Supported Development Platforms

The platform supports three tier-1 mobile architectures. Each stack is equipped with dedicated scaffolding templates, linting configurations, and enterprise SDK mirrors:

<Tabs>
  <TabItem label="React Native (New Architecture)">

Optimized for feature velocity and high code reuse (80%+ default enterprise standard). Leverages Fabric native renderer, TurboModules, and internal TypeScript packages.

* **Renderer:** Fabric C++ direct native engine
* **Module Architecture:** JSI & TurboModules (zero async bridge serialization)
* **Default State Engine:** Zustand + TanStack Query

<a href={`${PORTAL_BASE}/development-platforms/react-native/`}>View React Native Architecture Guide &rarr;</a>

  </TabItem>
  <TabItem label="Native Android (Kotlin / Compose)">

Engineered for hardware-intensive workflows, offline background sync daemons, Bluetooth peripherals, and deep Android OS integrations.

* **Language:** Kotlin 1.9+ with Coroutines & Structured Concurrency
* **UI Toolkit:** Jetpack Compose (Declarative)
* **Dependency Injection:** Hilt & Dagger 2

<a href={`${PORTAL_BASE}/development-platforms/android/`}>View Native Android Architecture Guide &rarr;</a>

  </TabItem>
  <TabItem label="Native iOS (Swift / SwiftUI)">

Tailored for flagship Apple ecosystem experiences requiring native Metal graphics, CoreML acceleration, secure enclave operations, or advanced iOS system integrations.

* **Language:** Swift 5.9+ with Swift Concurrency (`async/await`, Actors, `@MainActor`)
* **UI Toolkit:** SwiftUI
* **Security Enclave:** iOS Keychain Services & Biometric Gating

<a href={`${PORTAL_BASE}/development-platforms/ios/`}>View Native iOS Architecture Guide &rarr;</a>

  </TabItem>
</Tabs>

---

## Quality and Security Gates

Every production application binary progresses through a strict, automated verification pipeline before release approval:

1. **Pull Request Validation:** Branch rules require all code to branch from and target `main` via short-lived feature branches.
2. **Code Review:** Mandatory minimum of two passing reviews from code owners before merge.
3. **Bitrise & Danger Bot:** Automated checks analyze bundle size deltas, verify conventional commit syntax, and enforce changelog updates.
4. **Functional Testing (Sauce Labs):** Automated regression suites run across physical Android and iOS devices, validating UI state under varying battery, connectivity, and OS versions. Minimum 80% coverage required.
5. **Security Scanning (NowSecure):** Automated SAST/DAST detects insecure data storage, hardcoded secrets, and network communication vulnerabilities.
6. **Release Gate:** Staged rollout to test flights, enterprise internal portals, or public app stores.

---

## Engineering Domains

The documentation portal is organized into core technical domains that collectively support the mobile engineering lifecycle:

<MermaidZoom title="ENTERPRISE ENGINEERING DOMAINS">

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Mob["Enterprise Mobile Engineering Ecosystem"]

    subgraph Found["Foundations & Platforms"]
        D1["Architecture & Standards\n(Clean Architecture & Circuit Breaker)"]
        D2["Client Stacks & SDKs\n(Compose, SwiftUI, React Native)"]
    end

    subgraph Pipeline["Build & Security Pipeline"]
        D3["Build & Release CI/CD\n(Bitrise Pipelines & Code Signing)"]
        D4["Security & Compliance\n(NowSecure SAST/DAST & TGRC)"]
    end

    subgraph Delivery["Distribution & Enablement"]
        D5["App Distribution & Stores\n(Public Stores & Enterprise Internal)"]
        D6["Developer Productivity\n(Doctor Diagnostic CLI & Templates)"]
    end

    Mob --> Found
    Mob --> Pipeline
    Mob --> Delivery
```

</MermaidZoom>

* **Architecture & Standards:** Clean Architecture patterns, unidirectional data flow, Circuit Breaker resilience, and remote feature flag governance.
