## The Mental Model Shift: Web & Backend vs. Mobile

Engineers entering mobile from web or backend microservices often encounter subtle architectural differences that lead to major production bugs if unaddressed:

| Engineering Dimension | Web / Backend Architecture | Mobile Client Architecture | Why It Matters |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Runtime Environment** | Controlled servers or browser JS sandbox; predictable memory and CPU. | Heterogeneous mobile hardware (iOS & Android devices) with strict battery and RAM limits. | OS forcefully terminates apps that consume excessive RAM or background CPU. |
| **Deployment & Rollback** | Instant continuous deployment. Fixes deploy to production servers in minutes. | Compiled binaries (`.aab` / `.ipa`) distributed through App Store and Google Play. | Zero instant rollbacks. App store reviews take 24–72 hours; users must manually download updates. |
| **Execution & Threading** | Multi-threaded web servers or single-threaded event loop with async I/O. | Strict Main/UI thread (16.6ms frame budget). Background tasks require explicit dispatching. | Heavy computation on the Main Thread freezes the screen and triggers OS ANRs / app watchdog kills. |
| **Network Topology** | Reliable low-latency datacenter LAN or stable home broadband. | Volatile cellular connectivity, tunnel cutouts, subway dead zones, and sudden airplane mode. | Apps must be designed offline-first. Unhandled network drops cause immediate crashes or empty states. |
| **State & Lifecycle** | Stateless microservices or persistent browser tab until closed. | Transient OS lifecycle: Foreground &rarr; Background &rarr; Suspended &rarr; Process Death. | The OS can terminate background processes at any time; apps must restore state on relaunch. |
| **Security & Secrets** | Secrets stored securely in server-side environment variables or HashiCorp Vault. | Code and assets reside on user hardware. Binaries can be decompiled and inspected. | Never hardcode API keys or secrets in client code. Use Secure Enclave / KeyStore. |

