## Comprehensive Platform Evaluation Matrix

Compare the technical trade-offs across all three tier-1 supported stacks:

| Evaluation Dimension | React Native (New Architecture) | Native Android (Kotlin / Compose) | Native iOS (Swift / SwiftUI) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Enterprise Recommendation** | **Default Recommended (80%+ Apps)** | Hardware & Rugged Scenarios | Flagship Apple Ecosystem |
| **Code Reuse** | 90%–95% shared logic, UI, and test suites across iOS & Android. | 0% (Android only). Dual team required for iOS. | 0% (iOS only). Dual team required for Android. |
| **Time to Market** | Fastest delivery velocity. Single sprint backlog and shared components. | Moderate. Requires dedicated native Android specialists. | Moderate. Requires dedicated native iOS specialists. |
| **UI Engine** | Fabric C++ Native Renderer with Yoga Flexbox layout. | Jetpack Compose declarative layout engine. | SwiftUI declarative layout engine. |
| **Hardware & Bluetooth** | High-level BLE via TurboModules. Custom C++ native bindings. | Direct access to Android OS APIs, Bluetooth Classic, USB/OTG, and NDK. | Direct access to CoreBluetooth, ExternalAccessory, and Metal. |
| **Runtime & Startup** | Near-native cold boot via Hermes bytecode pre-compilation. | Native ART runtime ahead-of-time (AOT) compilation. | Native binary compiled directly to ARM64 machine instructions. |
| **Design System Mirroring** | Native JSX design tokens from `@enterprise/ui-tokens`. | Composable design tokens via Material 3 theme wrapper. | SwiftUI Color/Typography tokens via asset catalog. |
| **CI/CD Complexity** | Single Bitrise pipeline building both `.aab` and `.ipa`. | Gradle runner building `.aab`. | macOS runner building signed `.ipa`. |


