## When to Use the Native Escape Hatch (TurboModules)

Choosing **React Native** does not lock you out of native device capabilities. When high-performance hardware drivers or proprietary native SDKs are required, write a lightweight **TurboModule** in C++ or Swift/Kotlin rather than rewriting the application:

```typescript
// Specifying a Type-Safe TurboModule in React Native (TypeScript Spec)
import type { TurboModule } from 'react-native';
import { TurboModuleRegistry } from 'react-native';

export interface Spec extends TurboModule {
  // Direct C++ JSI call into native hardware driver without JSON bridge serialization
  scanBarcodeHardware(timeoutMs: number): Promise<string>;
  getBatteryHealth(): Promise<number>;
}

export default TurboModuleRegistry.getEnforcing<Spec>('EnterpriseHardwareScanner');
```

